    "done_when": "per §14's on-host comment: before any ssh call create /tmp/sshwrap/ssh as a script that execs /usr/bin/ssh -F $HOME/.ssh/config with all arguments, chmod +x it, export PATH=/tmp/sshwrap:$PATH, and run ssh -o BatchMode=yes jt-60sa hostname as a positive control; then on the host list every file under /analysis/src/getseldata_v4.2 (all extensions, includes and headers included) and grep them for JLOOP, JTPRB and JNPRB case-insensitively, reading only; compare the file list with the CodeFile rows under that prefix at facility jt-60sa in the graph and name every file on the host the graph does not hold; write the evidence fragment with the host file count, the graph file count, the files only on the host, and every array mention with its file and line, stating whether any file outside the graph fills the arrays; scripts and raw output in /home/ITER/mcintos/.config/reckon/crew/reports/imas-codex/getseldata-onhost-grep/; if the positive control fails, report the hop down and stop; no graph write, no code change, no discover run",
